{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And they complained.</b> From the nif'al conjugation, like וְיִכֹּנוּ (Proverbs 16:3), from נָכוֹנוּ (ibid. 19:29), from the doubled verbs [ Mediae nun ], or from עֲלוּמֵי הָעַיִן, and if it were from possessors of the letter nun it would be on the pattern of וַיִּגָּשׁוּ."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The phrase עֲלוֹמֵי הָעַיִן (literally 'concealments of the eye') is rendered hyper-literally; its grammatical referent is obscure."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:52.840432570Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}